#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:954
#, no-c-format
msgid "<glossterm>&DCOP;</glossterm>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:955
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The interprocess communication protocol used in &kde;. Short for Desktop "
"COmmunication Protocol."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:960
#, no-c-format
msgid "desktop"
msgstr "burèu"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:961
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&GNU;/&Linux;, FreeBSD and other systems that run X-Windows have multiple "
"desktops. You typically have four different desktops installed by default. "
"Each desktop can display its own set of programs and files. When &kde; first "
"starts up, the desktop you see is Desktop 1. If you press <keycombo action="
"\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo>, you will see Desktop 2. "
"Pressing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>F1</keycap></keycombo> will "
"bring back Desktop 1."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:971
#, no-c-format
msgid "history"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:972
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If &karm; is configured to log history, it will record ever start/stop timer "
"event. This history is never cleared when times are reset cleared and "
"remains on file until the task is deleted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:977
#, no-c-format
msgid "session"
msgstr "sesilha"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:978
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A user-defined starting point for the session timers. A new session begins "
"when you select <menuchoice> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Start New "
"Session</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. Session data is not saved when you "
"create a new session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: glossterm
#: index.docbook:988
#, no-c-format
msgid "system tray"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:989
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The system tray is in the bar that (by default) appears at the bottom of the "
"screen. In this system tray <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"systray.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> </inlinemediaobject> "
"the &karm; icon is on the far right."
msgstr ""

